{"public_message": "Ben, thanks. That was a direct answer, and it eases the concern I raised about your intro. Sarah, Emily and Arvin, thank you for taking my hypothetical too.

Maya, a small correction: Arvin, Sarah, Ben, Dr. Gordon and I have already answered both of your questions, and Elena answered the money one. Only Marcus and Emily are still outstanding, so let's not loop the whole room again.

Marcus, four or five of us have now asked you the same thing: what made you call three people quiet when they had already spoken? It's the one concrete oddity we have this round, and I'd like to hear your answer before I vote. If there's a simple explanation, such as posting before you'd read the thread, just say so. Right now my vote leans your way, mainly because the question is still unanswered, and I'm open to changing it.", "private_message_to": "Maya Rose", "private_message": "Maya, you already have my detail (the correspondence chess game). My honest read: I don't know yet. The only concrete thing is Marcus naming three 'quiet' people who had already spoken and then not responding when asked about it. Ben's first post was thin, but his follow-up was solid. I'm holding my vote until Marcus answers. Who looks like they're performing to you?", "notes_update": "Round 1 update: Ben recovered with a direct, substantive answer (said as holder he'd want everyone busy with tests while he coasted), so less suspicious. Marcus still hasn't answered the 'quiet' question that Emily, Ben, Sarah, Elena and I all asked, and he's my leading vote unless he explains well. Maya re-asked people who had already answered (inattentive, or just managing the room?). She keeps steering, so keep watching her. Emily hasn't answered Maya's two questions and Elena only answered the money one, both arguing details aren't checkable. Sarah is very thorough and process-focused. I told Maya privately that I have no firm read and lean Marcus. Details I've given: correspondence chess with college roommate (currently losing), mortgage plus Patagonia trek with Alex and the kids.", "done": false}

